{
  "verso": "1.1",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Titanic passenger list",
    "defaultKernel": "csharp"
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "3437cebc-236d-4310-9d66-69bd316996fd",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "# The Titanic passenger list\n\nEach block below is one step of a pipeline that prepares the passenger list for a network: it reads the file beside\nthis notebook, declares the columns that take part, splits the passengers into training, validation and test rows,\nand learns everything it learns from the training rows alone. **Show the data here** on any block shows the rows as\nthey stand there, each marked with the part it lands in."
    },
    {
      "id": "91c85803-90fd-4c8c-a48a-c4a96ea49d12",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022read.csv\u0022,\n  \u0022path\u0022: \u0022data/titanic.csv\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "b814958d-9efb-4918-a2a3-c6b12ebf522e",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022declare\u0022,\n  \u0022remainder\u0022: \u0022drop\u0022,\n  \u0022columns\u0022: [\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022survived\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: false\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022sibsp\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: false\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022parch\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: false\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022pclass\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022category\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: false\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022sex\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022category\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: false\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022age\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022number\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: true\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022name\u0022: \u0022fare\u0022,\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022number\u0022,\n      \u0022optional\u0022: false\n    }\n  ]\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "2f93bce4-ec04-499d-aaab-0841b5b0f2bd",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022split.stratified\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022survived\u0022,\n  \u0022train\u0022: 0.7,\n  \u0022validation\u0022: 0.15,\n  \u0022test\u0022: 0.15,\n  \u0022predict\u0022: 0,\n  \u0022seed\u0022: 20260923\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "684279f6-b903-43b6-9a88-a3282a3dcba7",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022target\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022survived\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "479a677b-101c-49c4-85c3-bc67bed7836d",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022fill.missing\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022age\u0022,\n  \u0022with\u0022: \u0022median\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "84b04f81-48df-422c-bf97-84ce86c2bf80",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022encode.categories\u0022,\n  \u0022as\u0022: \u0022onehot\u0022,\n  \u0022unseen\u0022: \u0022reserve\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "00a0ce4d-4e16-4464-ada5-5f3204a5fab9",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022normalise\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022age\u0022,\n  \u0022scale\u0022: \u0022midrange\u0022,\n  \u0022outOfRange\u0022: \u0022pass\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "67bef2ba-1304-41ce-915f-249425b736bb",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022normalise\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022fare\u0022,\n  \u0022scale\u0022: \u0022midrange\u0022,\n  \u0022outOfRange\u0022: \u0022pass\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "380aeda8-8261-43b5-9638-717d4f1353ff",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022normalise\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022sibsp\u0022,\n  \u0022scale\u0022: \u0022midrange\u0022,\n  \u0022outOfRange\u0022: \u0022pass\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "41c414db-0b06-4047-89dc-4f79a104a607",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022normalise\u0022,\n  \u0022column\u0022: \u0022parch\u0022,\n  \u0022scale\u0022: \u0022midrange\u0022,\n  \u0022outOfRange\u0022: \u0022pass\u0022\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "b3c23145-fafa-40ad-9d25-9f431d8b14f5",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022evidence.report\u0022,\n  \u0022metrics\u0022: [\n    \u0022accuracy\u0022,\n    \u0022precision\u0022,\n    \u0022recall\u0022,\n    \u0022confusionmatrix\u0022\n  ],\n  \u0022parts\u0022: [\n    \u0022validation\u0022,\n    \u0022test\u0022\n  ],\n  \u0022shown\u0022: [\n    \u0022numbers\u0022,\n    \u0022drawn\u0022\n  ]\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c",
      "type": "deepsharp.step",
      "source": "{\n  \u0022step\u0022: \u0022learn.network\u0022,\n  \u0022layers\u0022: [\n    {\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022dense\u0022,\n      \u0022units\u0022: 16\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022relu\u0022\n    },\n    {\n      \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022dense\u0022,\n      \u0022units\u0022: 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \u0022optimizer\u0022: {\n    \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022adam\u0022,\n    \u0022rate\u0022: 0.01,\n    \u0022firstMoment\u0022: 0.9,\n    \u0022secondMoment\u0022: 0.999,\n    \u0022epsilon\u0022: 1e-07\n  },\n  \u0022loss\u0022: {\n    \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022binaryCrossEntropy\u0022\n  },\n  \u0022stopping\u0022: {\n    \u0022kind\u0022: \u0022patience\u0022,\n    \u0022patience\u0022: 10,\n    \u0022least\u0022: 0,\n    \u0022best\u0022: true\n  },\n  \u0022engine\u0022: \u0022light\u0022,\n  \u0022seed\u0022: 20260929,\n  \u0022epochs\u0022: 100,\n  \u0022batch\u0022: 32\n}"
    },
    {
      "id": "bdd256b4-093f-4322-9fad-0478e63b1682",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": "The last block names the network these rows are prepared for: its layers, what moves them, what judges them and when the run stops. The block before it names what that network is measured by. The C# cell below trains exactly the network the blocks name \u2014 it reads the pipeline they hand over, after **Show the data here** on any block or the toolbar\u0027s run, trains it, and hands back what it predicted. **Show the data here** on the report block then draws the report under its grid."
    },
    {
      "id": "19abdf82-ed61-49d8-bcd7-693783ebffc4",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "source": "#r \u0022nuget: DeepSharp.Learners.Networks\u0022\n#r \u0022nuget: DeepSharp.Charts\u0022\nusing DeepSharp.Charts;\nusing DeepSharp.Learners.Networks;\nusing DeepSharp.Pipelines;\n\n// The pipeline the blocks declare, as text, run over the rows beside this notebook and trained as it says.\nvar text = Variables.Get\u003Cstring\u003E(\u0022deepsharp.pipeline\u0022);\nvar folder = Variables.TryGet\u003Cstring\u003E(\u0022deepsharp.folder\u0022, out var saved) ? SourceFolder.Of(saved) : SourceFolder.WorkingDirectory;\nvar declaration = PipelineDeclaration.FromJson(text, StepCatalog.BuiltIn().WithNetworks());\nvar trained = new Pipeline(declaration, rows: null, folder).Train();\n\n// What the report block measures and draws: the network\u0027s predictions, handed back as text.\nVariables.Set(\u0022deepsharp.predictions\u0022, trained.Measures!.PredictionsToJson());\n\ntrained.History!.LossCurve()"
    }
  ]
}